  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Jana
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Jana
  LastName: Sokolova
  Nickname: Janka
  Occupation: Florist
  CharacterDescription: Jana is thirty years old and wears a white wedding dress
    every day. The dress has been mended in several places and smells faintly of
    dried flowers. She never acknowledges that her outfit is unusual, but if asked
    about it directly she will give a different reason each time. She was at a fitting.
    She is the maid of honour. She simply likes it. There is a ceremony later. None
    of the explanations are consistent and she does not seem to notice. She makes
    extended eye contact and then looks away very suddenly. She does not like being
    asked questions and will sometimes answer a different question than the one posed
    to her. She is not hostile. She smiles often. Something is not right.
  CharacterArc: Jana worked as a florist in the residential district for six years,
    arranging bouquets for funerals, birthdays, and one wedding that did not happen.
    The details of that wedding change depending on who is asking, and Jana herself
    gives a different account each time she is prompted. By the early days of the
    crisis she had already been wearing the dress for some time. She moves through
    the checkpoint routine with a strange fluency, producing documents at the right
    moment and signing her name in clear letters, as if the procedural world still
    makes complete sense to her even when nothing else does. As the crisis deepens
    she becomes harder to read. Her explanations grow stranger and more elaborate.
    By the final days she no longer attempts explanations at all. She simply smooths
    the skirt of the dress and waits, very patiently, for something that is not coming.
  DateOfBirth: 22/06/1993
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 22 JUN
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
