  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Thank you. You are very kind. There is a ceremony later. You should come.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Thank you. I will remember your face. I remember every face.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Good. Good. I knew you would understand. Not everyone does.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Oh. All right. Could someone call, no, never mind. I will wait. I am good at
      waiting.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I do not understand. I have my papers. I always have my papers. I have my papers.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Please. I have somewhere to be. Please. It will not take long.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "But the\u2026 I was supposed to\u2026 the flowers are\u2026"
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I only needed to get home. That is all. I only needed to get home.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "Oh\u2026 I see\u2026 that is\u2026 that is all right then\u2026 it is fine\u2026"
  quarantineExitLines:
  - I am not sick. I am just wearing a dress. People wear dresses.
  - Could someone water my plants? I have plants at home. They need water every second
    day.
  - Is there a window? I would like to see outside. I like to see if it is raining.
  killExitLines:
  - "I thought\u2026 I was sure there was still time\u2026"
  - I did not understand. I had my papers. I had everything right.
  - "Is the ceremony\u2026 will someone tell them I\u2026 tell them I tried to\u2026"
  voiceAudioClips: []
  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c73bcde73ca45b24c870219573f99a55, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Home. I was home all morning. I had to air out the dress.
    midDaysAnswer: The dry cleaner. They said they could not help with the stain.
      I am not sure what stain. I did not see one.
    finalDaysAnswer: I do not remember exactly. I walked for a while. I ended up
      here.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The ceremony hall. East side, past the transit stop.
      Very nice hall. Big windows.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The florist. She had everything ready. Beautiful arrangements.
      White and ivory.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I was at the venue. Confirming details. The ceremony
      is very soon now.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: No. I feel completely fine. I have felt fine for a long time.
    midDaysAnswer: I lose track of things sometimes. Days. Not days. Smaller things.
      I do not think that is a symptom.
    finalDaysAnswer: I cannot always remember what I came to do. But I remember where
      I am going. Usually.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: No symptoms at all. Very clear head. Perfect memory.
      I remember everything in order.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Nothing unusual. Very steady. I have been sleeping very
      well. No confusion at all.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I am completely fine. Very sharp. I know exactly where
      I have been and why.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Alone. For now. That will change soon.
    midDaysAnswer: Just me. I used to have a cat. She is gone now.
    finalDaysAnswer: Alone. I have lived alone for a while. It is fine. I prefer
      it.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: "My fianc\xE9. He is at home right now. He is getting
      ready. We are both getting ready."
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: We live together. He and I. He is very good. He does not
      go out much anymore.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: We are both there. In the apartment. He is waiting for
      me right now. I should not be long.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - I know you are not supposed to ask about the dress. Most people do not ask.
    - There is a ceremony soon. I am told to stay ready. So I stay ready.
    - I have been through this checkpoint many times. You get used to the smell.
    midDays:
    - The dress holds its shape well. Considering. I have had it a long time.
    - I once asked someone here what day it was. He told me. It was not the day I
      thought it was.
    - I do not mind waiting. I have been waiting for quite a while now. A little
      longer is nothing.
    finalDays:
    - Do you think it will rain? I cannot get the dress very wet. I have already
      had it cleaned once.
    - Everyone always looks at the dress first. I understand. It is a very white
      dress.
    - I have been counting the days. I stopped when I lost count. It was a high number.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
